  "cover_text": "Headed over to the O.co Coliseum for the Oakland Engineers' 7 p.m. ET first scrimmage before the opening game Monday night, the Warriors might be feeling familiar — sporting a band, some empty seats in front of the bars and the smell of stale pizza.\nOff the start line anyway, the Warriors are now 6-0 this season and have been surprisingly close to catching up to the reigning defending champs — Bengals — on the road. Tonight’s opening game will be an exhibition in defeat.\nSince hitting the college basketball scene in 2008, Oakland has the longest running record for an all-appearance opening game as well as best road record for a home game — the Black and White rattling off 10-",
